{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"usa patriot act\" (+ \"357-66\" \"357 to 66\" \"357–66\") (+ \"98-1\" \"98 to 1\" \"98–1\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1393034455#0_2889021612","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q794","rank":3,"snippet":"a key part - and often the leading role - in a number of successful operations to protect innocent Americans from the deadly plans of terrorists dedicated to destroying America and our way of life. While the results have been important, in passing the Patriot Act, Congress provided for only modest, incremental changes in the law. Congress simply took existing legal principles and retrofitted them to preserve the lives and liberty of the American people from the challenges posed by a global terrorist network. PDF version The USA PATRIOT Act: Preserving Life and Liberty (Uniting and Strengthening America by Providing Appropriate Tools Required to Intercept and Obstruct Terrorism) Congress enacted the Patriot Act by overwhelming, bipartisan margins, arming law enforcement with new tools to detect and prevent terrorism: The <cover>USA Patriot Act was passed nearly unanimously by the Senate 98-1, and 357-66 </cover>in the House, with the support of members from across the political spectrum. The Act Improves Our Counter-Terrorism Efforts in Several Significant Ways:\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"\" , \"url\": \"https://www.justice.gov/archive/ll/highlights.htm\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_17747056#1_34930249","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_17747056#2_34931921","rank":2,"relevance":3}]}}
