{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"patriot act\" (+ \"large majorities\" \"overwhelming margin\" \"lopsided vote\" \"bipartisan margins\") (+ \"house\" \"senate\") (+ \"357\" \"66\" \"98\" \"1\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_3267792029#2_3606719341","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q816","rank":7,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.<cover>1_doc_16_3267792029#2_3606719341\" , \"end_char\": 3710.000000 , \"headings\": \"Controversial invocations of the Patriot Act Controversial invocations of the Patriot Act Contents Dismissal of United States Attorneys Investigating copyright infringement Investigation of potential drug traffickers Blanket requests for financial, library, and other information on visitors to Las Vegas Wrongful accusations under the Act Controversial requests to the media Other cases Lawsuits Klayman v. Obama Others See also References \" , \"segment\": \"Critics have claimed the dismissals were either motivated by desire to install attorneys more loyal to the Republican party or as retribution for actions or inactions damaging to the Republican party. At least six of the eight had positive internal Justice Department performance reports. A bill, S-214, filed in January 2007, to rescind the no-term-limit interim U.S. attorney provision was approved by very large majorities in both the Senate </cover>and the House, and was signed into law by the President on June 14, 2007, designated Public Law No: 110-34 and called the Preserving United States Attorney Independence Act ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1411283596#2_2892646769","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1411283596#1_2892645254","rank":2,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1393034455#1_2889023579","rank":3,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_1662414130#2_1782379673","rank":4,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1393034455#0_2889021612","rank":5,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_641525144#2_1418396067","rank":6,"relevance":2}]}}
