{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"patriot act\" (+ \"little debate\" \"few members\" \"read the bill\" \"48 hours\") (+ \"357\" \"66\" \"98\" \"1\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1959226880#1_3173288113","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q819","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1959226880#<cover>1_3173288113\" , \"end_char\": 1951.000000 , \"headings\": \"What is the USA Patriot Act? What is the USA Patriot Act?\" , \"segment\": \"The USA Patriot Act is composed of 342 pages. Most lawmakers admit that they never read the bill </cover>before voting on it. Put simply, from October 23 to October 26, a massive piece of legislation was rammed through both the House of Representatives and Senate, without public hearings of any sort. It was sold as the legal measures required to prevent future terroristic attacks on U.S. soil. In the wake of the September 11, 2001, attacks, the American people were gripped in fear. Any and all measures of self-protection seemed desirable. But in the hysteria, the President, aided and abetted by both houses of the federal legislature, violated the U.S. Constitution and, in turn, stripped away the basic civil liberties embodied in the Bill of Rights, in the name of \"national security.\" The USA Patriot Act (PA) is composed of many laws already on the books that "}}
{"request":{"judgments":"38/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1959226880#1_3173288113","relevance":1,"reason":"This page is about the USA PATRIOT Act and discusses its rapid passage and claims many lawmakers did not read the 342-page bill, but it does not provide exact congressional support or vote totals.","learned":"Some critical narratives emphasize the Patriot Act's rapid passage and limited deliberation, but this snippet lacks the House/Senate vote counts."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q819","reason":"The rapid-passage/limited-debate query may still return criticism-oriented sources that include the lopsided House and Senate vote totals, so continue to the next result."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q819"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_09_913747125#3_1553005489","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q819","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.<cover>1_doc_09_913747125#3_1553005489\" , \"end_char\": 1900.000000 , \"headings\": \"The Government Is Watching Us The Government Is Watching Us Join millions of other students and start your research Become a StudyMode Member \" , \"segment\": \"It should be known as the Constitution Shredding Act. One of the saddest things about this act is that many Americans do not even know anything about it. The act was also rushed through its process. With very little debate, it was passed. There wasn't even a report from the Senate regarding the act (Patriot Act). </cover>It is wrong of the government to pass laws without carefully analyzing each and every part of the law that they plan to put into effect. The government has many surveillance tactics. One of the tactics that the government uses is the Big Brother tactic. They use this in the library. The government monitors everything that people do in the library;\" , \"start_char\": 1236.000000 , \"title\": \"The Government Is Watching "}}
{"request":{"judgments":"39/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_09_913747125#3_1553005489","relevance":1,"reason":"This student/essay-style result is related to the Patriot Act and says it was rushed through with little debate, but it gives no exact support level or House/Senate vote totals.","learned":"Rapid-passage criticism can produce low-value results that discuss process but not how much congressional support the Patriot Act received."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"patriot act\" (+ \"voted against\" \"voted no\" \"opposed\") (+ house senate) (+ \"357\" \"66\" \"98\" \"1\" feingold))","reason":"Search from the opposition-count angle—who voted against or voted no—while requiring House/Senate and key numbers/Feingold, likely surfacing passages that directly imply or state the support totals."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"patriot act\" (+ \"voted against\" \"voted no\" \"opposed\") (+ house senate) (+ \"357\" \"66\" \"98\" \"1\" feingold))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_1045882057#4_1431587411","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q820","rank":4,"snippet":"Multi-Point (\"Roving Wiretap\") Authority Liberalized Use of Pen Register/Trap and Trace Devices under FISA Access to \"Any Tangible Things\" Sunset Provision Additional Amendments Providing Government the Authority to Combat Terrorism Amendments to Immigration Laws Resources News Articles USA PATRIOT Act Resources Previous Top News \" , \"segment\": \"The House Judiciary Committee voted to send the USA FREEDOM Act of 2015 to the House of Representatives for further consideration prior to the June <cover>1 Patriot Act expiration deadline. The bill would end the NSA's controversial domestic telephone record collection program. The bill would also establish new transparency requirements for Intelligence Court Orders, recommended by EPIC in testimony before the House Judiciary Committee. EPIC also opposed </cover>renewal of the NSA's Section 215 orders and petitioned the Supreme Court to suspend the program. ( May. 1, 2015) Senator McConnell Seeks Renewal of NSA Bulk Collection Program: Senate majority leader Mitch McConnell has introduced a bill that would extend the Patriot Act until 2020. Specifically, S. 1035 would renew the controversial Section 215 authorities for the NSA's telephone record collection program. The 215 authority is set to expire on June 1. EPIC urged the President and ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_593034728#0_869314168","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1778472344#3_2688093350","rank":2,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1778472344#2_2688091675","rank":3,"relevance":3}]}}
