{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1758288482#5_2640777282","relevance":1,"reason":"This HuffPost article about a 2011 Patriot Act extension gives a related public-opinion data point from Pew—34% felt the law went too far and threatened civil liberties—but it is not dedicated to the original support question and does not provide the congressional passage support totals or a clear support percentage.","learned":"A 2011 Pew poll cited in coverage of Patriot Act extension found 34% thought the law went too far and threatened civil liberties, suggesting divided public opinion on later extensions."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q826","reason":"Continue the public-opinion query briefly to see whether it returns dedicated polling sources with exact support percentages for the Patriot Act, an alternate interpretation of the information need."}}
